the breaking news that uh we can bring  you is that sanju javid  has been confirmed as the new health  secretary  our political correspondent is at  standing by in westminster  forest rob yes in many ways um i think  julian sajid javid was something of a  ready-made senior cabinet minister for  boris johnson  to pick and put into the health brief  without the need for any type of wider  reshuffle of course his last position in  the cabinet was that he took  on the role um as chancellor uh when  boris johnson moved into number 10 he  went into number 11.  he of course left that position over an  argument  about whether he should share his  advisory team with number 10 there'd  been a desire  for a shared team to work between number  10 and number 11.  that was received by sajid javid um at  the time  um as a sort of land grab by downing  street taking away  some of the independence and the power  that he would have  which is why he decided to resign and  rishi sunak  came in uh anyway that was 13th of  february  he resigned of course in the coming  weeks really  the world changed in terms of covid  rolling in and the role of the  chancellor  was morphed from what it had been before  as well before that he has a lot of  experience  in cabinet as well he was the business  secretary the culture secretary the  community secretary the home secretary  as well so someone with a lot of top  level  cabinet experience and he will need  every inch of it i think  if um he is going to uh succeed in this  very very  challenging brief because of course it's  not just the fallout  from covid and the pandemic that he will  have to deal with we're not  fully out of it yet but that we are also  going through the nhs is going through  a real pinch point and pressure point in  terms of catching up  with missed operations and missed  treatments then there is an extensive  program of reform that matt hancock  had set in motion in the past few months  to really reorganize  how the nhs runs and reverse many of the  reforms the lansley reforms pushed  through during the coalition years  under david cameron and then on top of  that remember the full title is not just  health secretary it's health  and social care secretary there is a  promised reform  and plan to social care that has been  long promised by many prime ministers  including boris johnson and never  delivered on  that is something that is getting  increased political heat in the recent  weeks  and that is something that will be right  at the top of sagitt javid's  in tray add into that the chief  executive of the nhs  simon stevens is also due to leave his  post  this summer that was something that was  far more long planned and not spurred on  by  any of uh similar reasons to the context  in which matt hancock left  so sadget javid will be coming in and  working with  a new chief executive of the nhs  at a point where the nhs has just gone  through the biggest challenge  it has potentially ever faced at a point  where they are standing  on the edge of a huge swathe of reforms  so this is potentially one of the most  uh daunting briefs in government at the  moment  and potentially one of the most daunting  appointments but he is someone with a  lot of experience he is someone that  when he left  government even though it was on the  back of  an argument around um with boris johnson  and downing street  about the makeup of his team and his  advisory team he made it very clear  at the time that he would be happy to  come back um  into government and that is what we are  seeing now putting put back in  one of the most prominent cabinet  positions  um at the moment and i think it will be  interesting to see whether he carries on  with uh those reforms that matt hancock  had started or whether he tries to go  um in a different direction but  i think any time cabinet positions open  up or there is rumors of a reshuffle  rumors  of sajid javid's return to office  circulate today was no different but  this time  they have proved to be true uh and he is  being brought  back into cabinet i imagine this does  suggest  that there won't be a wider reshuffle  that this will just be  um a single swap out and swap in uh  rather than anything more substantial  and uh rob in terms of um sajid javi  being a safe  pair of hands he has been out of cabinet  for  some time but is that generally how he's  regarded i think he is regarded um  in the current circumstances as probably  one of the safer pair of hands you could  put in  uh if you look at some of the other  names that have been floating around  there had been rumors about nadeem  zahawi the current vaccines minister  stepping up but that  nadim tahawi is someone that although uh  being involved in the very successful  vaccine program is someone with  uh no cabinet experience i believe and  only a few years of ministerial  experience so that would have been  a very big step up um for him  other names linked to it include michael  gove someone that when he has gone into  other departments including the  department for education  um has been proved to be someone that  although controversial in many ways  can actually get things done can  actually force through agendas  and i think that reputation for michael  gove is the reason why many people  linked him with health  somewhere where you are dealing with  huge huge institutions  and bags and bags of bags of red tape so  you really need  to be something of a political force in  order to bend all of that  to your will and try to push through  change that you want to see  ultimately though michael gove is in  another position with bigger challenges  on his plate  as well and maybe the calculation was in  number 10 that actually it was a lot  easier to put sachit javid in  i think on the whole as well it's not  necessarily a politically controversial  appointment you won't find i think too  many people um  feeling that their noses have been put  out of joint by this because he is  someone that has got so much cabinet  experience  and he is someone that is coming from  the outside um and back in so  uh yes i think in a way it seemed uh  like  the obvious choice both in the  circumstances and looking at sajid  javid's  cv but that's not to say this is going  to be  an easy job for him also he is someone  that doesn't  really come with too much baggage and i  think  that was important to put someone in in  that position  where there is no potential chance  of anything going wrong in the same vein  that it has gone wrong  with matt hancock so i think an  indication that they wanted  they didn't want this to be long and  drawn out they didn't want this to be a  long  reshuffle in downing street they wanted  this to be a quick changeover  and i expect the messaging that will be  put out by  the government um this evening and in  the coming days will be this is all  about  uh a sort of seamless transition this is  all about continuing  with the vaccine program this is all  about reopening uh  next month july the 19th that final  terminus date as it has been known  and this is not about wider  reorganization this is about putting  someone in  who has cabinet experience that is seen  as a safe pair of hands  to carry on where matt hancock has  left off  okay rob um just in terms of the the  reshuffle that had been muted that it  was something that boris johnson  was thinking of but this obviously  circumvents that and there's no need  it's a  one bringing in a minister who hasn't  been in cabinet  and therefore there isn't the need to  reshuffle everybody else so it is a  a very simple one move yeah i think  reshuffles have been doing the rounds in  the westminster rumor mill  for weeks if not months now but this  does make it a lot more straightforward  i think the other thing that boris  johnson may have done  is move someone else like oliver dowd in  his culture secretary into health and  then backfill him with sajid javid in  the end he clearly felt  the cleanest and the easiest thing to do  was to bring someone in  who could just fill that vacancy without  the need  for any of the other reorganizations and  the headaches that can come  with that and in sagittar javid he has  someone  that has the cv to do that and someone  that i think  the party will probably receive on the  whole  fairly warmly

